// Title: OMeta: an object-oriented language for pattern matching
// Authors: Alessandro Warth, Ian Piumarta
// Source: VPRI Technical Report TR-2007-003 (2007), Figure 3 ("Extending Java with foreveryother loops").
//   PDF page 6 (of 10), top. Section 3.1 ("Quick and Easy Language Extensions").
// Transcribed from the page images; text-layer differences noted below.

meta Java++ <: Java {
  stmt ::= <space>* ’foreveryother’ <space>* ’(’ <expr>:x <space>* ’)’ <stmt>:s => ...
        | <super stmt>;
}

// Transcription notes
// - Checked at 300 dpi. The "..." after "=>" is three periods, printed as an unfinished semantic action.
// - Literal quotes are the right single quote U+2019 at both ends of each literal, matching the text layer.
// - Caption (not part of listing): "Extending Java with foreveryother loops."
